# --- Live append-only bot output -------------------------------------------------
# These files are written continuously by running bots. Tracking them meant a branch
# switch reverted them to their last commit, discarding everything appended since —
# which truncated MIM-NB's hash-chained audit trail on 2026-08-06 and destroyed two
# sessions outright (prereg sigma-provenance Amendment 3 §10.5). A file cannot be both
# a git-versioned artifact and a live append target. Same treatment as data/trades.db.
# Frozen one-off artifacts in these directories stay tracked via the negations.
data/mim_nb/*
!data/mim_nb/trades.csv.bak-*
data/gap_fade/*
!data/gap_fade/fills_backfill_report.csv
# Frozen provenance record for the 2026-08-06 loss, written once by
# tools/gap_fade_ledger_repair.py. Like fills_backfill_report.csv it is a one-shot
# artifact, not a live append target, so tracking it is safe and it belongs with the
# incident write-up it documents.
!data/gap_fade/ledger_repair_20260812.csv
data/combine_joint/*
data/ts_sim_mirror/*

# Exception to the data/processed/* rule above, recorded because it is deliberate.
# The frozen warmup series below is FORCE-ADDED and therefore tracked despite that rule
# (gitignore governs untracked files only). It is not bot output — it is a frozen input
# the sigma seed depends on for the pre-live era, and the corroboration on 2026-08-06
# established that the venue cannot substitute for it: TradeStation revises its own
# 1-minute history (145/390 bars differ on a session we can check). Losing or altering
# this file makes sigma's pre-2026-06-11 history unreconstructible.
#   data/processed/dollar_bars/1_minute/mnq_1min_2026_ytd.csv   (tracked, see above)
